Force the mt7925u (Netgear A8000 AXE3000, 0846:9072) 5 GHz band. Some
firmware builds report a hw_path capability bitmap without the 5 GHz bit
even though the MT7925 silicon is tri-band, which leaves only
NL80211_BAND_2GHZ registered and makes 5 GHz AP mode impossible. Force the
flag so the wiphy exposes the 5 GHz band.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mcu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mcu.c
@@ -908,3 +908,5 @@ mt7925_mcu_parse_phy_cap(struct mt792x_dev *dev, char *data)
 	mdev->phy.cap.has_2ghz = cap->hw_path & BIT(WF0_24G);
 	mdev->phy.cap.has_5ghz = cap->hw_path & BIT(WF0_5G);
+	/* Some 0846:9072 firmware reports a 2.4 GHz-only hw_path. */
+	mdev->phy.cap.has_5ghz = true;
 }
